those are the risks that this says you will tend to underestimate.

43
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:09,660
All right. Okay. Then there's

44
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:13,140
another common way of estimating probabilities,

45
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:17,260
and this is from comparing particular cases to stereotypes,

46
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:19,220
and then using the better match.

47
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:22,300
And this is known as the representative heuristic.

48
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:24,340
So, this is a different one.

49
00:01:24,340 --> 00:01:28,260
So, a standard example of this is,

50
00:01:28,260 --> 00:01:30,940
suppose someone asks you which is more likely?

51
00:01:30,940 --> 00:01:33,260
Is a Chinese professor who teaches Chinese literature,

52
00:01:33,260 --> 00:01:35,300
or a Chinese professor who teaches psychology?

53
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:36,940
All right. Well, what is

54
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:40,980
your stereotypical nationality for a professor of Chinese literature?

55
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:42,340
Chinese.

56
00:01:42,340 --> 00:01:46,780
What is your stereotypical nationality for a psychology professor?

57
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:50,580
American. American. Maybe Austrian or something.

58
00:01:50,580 --> 00:01:53,100
Zinken-Freud. All right.

59
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:56,580
Anyway. So, this one,

60
00:01:56,580 --> 00:01:59,340
certainly Chinese is not the nationality that you

61
00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:02,220
picture when you think of a psychology professor.

62
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:03,860
So, you're probably going to think, say,

63
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:06,380
all right, so, high likelihood that

64
00:02:06,380 --> 00:02:08,820
a Chinese professor is a professor of Chinese literature,

65
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:11,740
low likelihood that he's a professor of psychology.

66
00:02:11,740 --> 00:02:13,660
Now, what's wrong with this?

67
00:02:13,660 --> 00:02:15,660
Well, sometimes there's nothing wrong with it.

68
00:02:15,660 --> 00:02:18,380
But the problem is that in the real world,

69
00:02:18,380 --> 00:02:22,100
people tend to ignore what are called base rates.

70
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:27,220
So, here's the thing. How many professors of Chinese literature are there in America?

71
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:30,660
Very, very few.

72
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:33,020
